tation and that is  the reason why he let him go instead of  him just awkwardly staring at him and  not pursuing him but whatever we now  have to save leia again for the third  time and obi-wan asked rokan for help to  which he very strongly says no until he  goes on about his sob backstory and then  he immediately changes his mind without  any persuasion from obi-wan and he  agrees to help them wow how convenience  while this is all happening reeva is  interrogating leia and at one point she  finally uses her forced mind reading  ability leia being that she is force  sensitive is able to resist it and reiva  even admits that she is strong which  wouldn't this immediately throw up a red  flag for rava if you physically can't  read this child's mind then the only  possible explanation for that is that  she's force sensitive and that's why  she's resisting but this moment is  quickly brushed off and for how much  raven knows everything i'm surprised she  wasn't more suspicious of leia's force  capabilities this scene should have  played out where reva discovers that  leia is force sensitive and is about to  entomb leia before being saved by  obi-wan instead of him randomly walking  into the tomb and leia not actually  being there and it's like he's wasting  time as she's about to die or be  tortured but going back to obi-wan and  talo's initial infiltration it's pretty  tense especially for tala as she's  almost found out and has to reinforce  her higher rank to another guard however  there is always issues with these types  of infiltration scenes in which the  security detail seems extremely light  and there are never any security cameras  or why would he put a camera in this  droid that moves around and not in a  stationary position that has constant  coverage of said area and on the subject  of defense capabilities of fortress  inquisitorius they also have no aerial  defenses given that some air speeders  were able to do a strafing run on the  base or let alone the space having any  tie fighters on hands so if they get  attacked then they can't do anything i  guess  but going back to the infiltration  obi-wan finds a team of the fallen jedi  right away this feels like a leonardo  dicaprio pointing meme scene where fans  try to spot all the easter eggs which  raises the question how were all these  bodies captured in their final moments  did these inquisitors force freeze them  on death or are they not actually dead  did they put these jedi back into their  death poses i don't know and the team in  theory seems like a cool concept but in  execution there are a lot of questions  since they breeze over it so quickly and  it doesn't come back up again while  obi-wan is gawking at all these dead  bodies or maybe alive bodies lei is  about to be tortured or killed or  whatever and it's kind of funny to see  obi-wan's sense of urgency inevitably  though obi-wan saves leia and they catch  back up with tala and in order to get  leia out of the fortress obi-wan opts to  hide leia under his coats this has to be  the most ridiculous thing in the show  and from this alone it feels like the  writers are writing this for children  how does no one notice this obvious kid  hiding under a trench coat they're  walking past hundreds of stormtroopers  out in this massive room like what i  feel like this reinforces the notion  that stormtroopers are legally blind  then upon getting to the hangar rava  stops obi-wan from getting away which  immediately contradicts their plans of  letting them go and finding the ripple  network why we're stopping them and  recapturing them given that they are  surrounded by stormtroopers when you can  simply do nothing and achieve your  supposed goal but nope we need to have  an explosive escape sequence that again  showcases the utter incompetence of  stormtroopers and they get away now  another logical explanation is that reva  could have told everyone else to let  them go and that's why no one else  noticed a child under a trench coat but  that's not even the case because later  it's revealed she told noah her plans so  yeah this entire episode is a  devastating headache and the defense of  the rebel base is just as bad  the rebel outpost defense may be a bit  overshadowed by the cool darth vader  moment of him force grabbing a ship but  everything leading up to that moment is  pretty ridiculous starting with the  notion that leigh is now an engineer at  the age of 10 let alone lay at any point  in the original trilogy really  showcasing that ability and even after  scouring through the first three movies  the only moment i could find was her  briefly turning a lever in the  millennium falcon and empire strikes  back and that was it so this trend of  giving kid characters so many adult like  personality traits and skills is pretty  absurd and the second it happens you  immediately go  yeah right a 10 year old cannot do that  and it immediately breaks your immersion  and suspension of disbelief and it's  also kind of funny that everyone is  entirely dependent on this kid to fix  the issue so the amount of trust is  massive and is of course unrealistic  again  after that obi-wan gets a transmission  and gets interrupted by tala obi-wan  doesn't really say anything to her and  for whatever reason she starts to drone  on about her tragic backstory it  basically comes out of left field and i  immediately thought the writers are  trying to force the audience into a  sympathetic view of the character  right before they kill her off which is  exactly what happens  then rave inevitably breaks through the  door and somehow dozens of stormtroopers  managed to miss rebels barely hiding  behind cover like how is this possible  it's probably just as hard to miss given  that there are a bunch of rebels  standing out in the open  it's literally shooting fish in a barrel  but the stormtroopers can't even manage  that i know in the original trilogy they  had notoriously bad aim and i feel like  that was always george lucas giving his  heroes plot armor  which as a result the enemies always  missed but here disney's writers are  just running with the concept of  stormtroopers being utterly blinds and  it makes any action scene the right at  this point feel completely tensionless  and unintentionally comedic because to a  degree it's okay if they miss a bit but  to this extent that they're showing  right now it's way too far-fetched i i  just can't suspend my disbelief anymore  before opie wants to renders and talks  to rava he gives his stuff to hajja one  of the important items he gives to him  was the message he received from bail  organa talking about luke during their  sudden evacuation hajja drops it and  turns around to look at it and  apparently leaves it on the ground which  is so stupid and is such a contrived way  to have rava figure out this information  like obi-wan kenobi just gave you his  possessions and you drop it and don't  even care to pick it back up what then  it doesn't even stop there because  obi-wan tells rava that while darth  vader is focused on him she should take  him out to which she lets him go and i'm  assuming she wanted him to escape given  that there were only a couple  stormtroopers on him and he obviously  breaks it loose but the confusing bit is  that obi-wan just flat out leaves in the  ship without personally distracting  darth vader unless if darth vader  holding the ship was when rave was  supposed to attack and not after it  squandering her window of opportunity so  rafa suddenly turns into a dumb  character so that she could get skewered  and conveniently find the message that  haja dropped i already went into the  whole fiasco of her surviving but yeah  this whole sequence was very convoluted  and messy  before going into the finale let's  briefly touch on princess leia since  there are a lot of different aspects  surrounding her that are either  confusing or are written in a stupid  manner firstly let's look at her  characteristics as a 10 year old because  young lia feels like she's written by a  middle-aged man who doesn't know how  kids act mentally she is like an adult  and any soon she has with obi-wan she's  basically always running circles around  him and bossing him around not to  mention her being witty and charismatic  all of these characteristics packed into  a 10 year old flat out doesn't work it  comes across as disney wanting young  lady to inspire kids however you can do  that without overloading her to the  point where she starts to become a mary  sue because at that age she shouldn't be  able to evade bounty hunters in obi-wan  kenobi being able to intelligently think  her way out of situations when obi-wan  seemingly can't in comparison and even  being a mechanic it feels like this is  written for kids when star wars should  have an all-encompassing age demographic  let alone the obi-wan vs darth vader's  story being really dark which some dark  elements bleed through like darth vader  torturing obi-wan but then that's  immediately contrasted against leia  having her comedic chase scene then  there's also the notorious retcon for  leia wearing a new hope leia's message  said this and i can't play the clip  because there's copyrighted music so she  says general kenobi years ago you served  my father in the clone wars now he begs  you to serve him in a struggle against  the empire so this line in her message  to obi-wan indicates that she doesn't  know him and instead knows her as this  man who served her father in the clone  wars which you'd think that leia going  on a massive adventure with obi-wan  would at least be somewhat memorable so  this doesn't really line up with a new  hope in terms of this being a problem  it's not that big of a deal but since  this retcon exists it will forever feel  like latest time when the show is forced  and there's also another small retcon i  found in rogue one where bail organa  mentions obi wan  friend  jedi he served me well during the clone  wars and he's lived in hiding to the  emperor's purge yes i will send for him  yeah i don't think he's exactly been  living and hiding considering he just  saved an entire group of rebels leia and  fought darth vader twice so far and it  seems like disney wants to continue on  with this  and then lastly i'll touch on the final  episode since this is the most recent  thing that came out  now this is by far the best episode for  obvious reasons however there is one  aspect that really drags down the  enjoyment which is that each of the  climactic scenes are shrouded in  darkness especially for a tv setup  because man did i have a hard time  seeing what was happening before  rewatching it on my monitor now the  devordologic aspect stems from the fact  that this show reportedly has a budget  of about 25 million dollars an episode  so it's mind boggling that their  creators chose to have these scenes take  place at night with no dynamic light  sources besides their lightsabers it  doesn't really come across as being that  expensive to produce on top of the fact  that no lightsaber fights take place in  that good of a set piece in comparison  to the films from the concept art i  thought they would hearken back to  revenge of the sith and incorporate some  lava but that never showed up if  anything when darth vader did his  awesome earthquake force move i thought  he could at least reveal some lava to  light up the scene which unfortunately  doesn't happen then for rave's emotional  scene you can barely see her given that  her entire costume is black so she's  almost invisible and for a second i  didn't even realize she was crying then  despite the action and choreography  being great for darth vader and  obi-wan's fight scene the editing is  sometimes jarring which again goes  towards the 25 million budget and i'm  really confused why they couldn't have  cleaner action with longer takes  especially since they are already  cutting corners by having very limited  light  then for one other devotologic aspect  about the finale that really bothered me  was how incompetent the star destroyer  was i guess they also have terrible aim  now and shouldn't they also have tie  fighters why do they have to make the  choice to go after one of the ships just  deploy a squadron on one and keep the  star destroyer on the other but yeah i  covered the main issues with the show  and there are still dozens of small  writing mistakes splintering throughout  the show like obi-wan going out of his  way to disable a laser gate when he can  simply walk around it or these guards  clearly seeing obi-wan sneaking around  but they have plot armor obstructing  their vision i could go on for a while  but the video is already getting long  and i feel like i've already proven my  point of how poorly written some aspects  of the show are thank you for watching  and i assume most people who have  disliked this video probably already  left so thank you for sticking around
 

